{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe","id":1083058,"title":"Are the Stargazers a needed tribe?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-24T09:51:51-07:00","id":1083058,"title":"Are the Stargazers a needed tribe?","content":"I came to WtA very late, at the end of Revised in fact. So I never truly got to experience the Stargazers in a major way.<br /> <br /> However, I have read a lot about them, including both tribebooks. And, well, I cannot help but feel they never truly added to the game anything new. Aside from Kailindo.<br /> <br /> They are an asian tribe, but even in 1st edition Shadow Lords all ready had Hakken in Japan. They basically are monks in a search for enlightement and so they are calm and collected. They eschew posessions and ties and dislike the Weaver strongly.<br /> <br /> To me, that doesn't really sound werewolfy at all. Especially when the focus is so heavily on the human aspects, with a much lessened focus on the wolf. I mean, that is true with all idealistic tribes, but generally there is a secondary thing for lupus to chomp on. It doesn't help that Gazers generally are portrayed as somehow perfect, when even the Children of Gaia get called on tokenism in the books.<br /> <br /> And they offer very little that Children of Gaia or Uktena couldn't offer.<br /> <br /> I don't know, I just feel that them leaving in revised did not actually matter as much as if say the Fenrir or Furies had left.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T11:00:47-07:00","id":1083093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe#post1083058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't know, I just feel that them leaving in revised did not actually matter as much as if say the Fenrir or Furies had left.</div> </div> </div> </div> Eh. I think you could drop any individual Tribe and it wouldn't effect the overall Setting all that much. That being said, I see your point.<br /> <br /> They were just about the smallest Tribe anyway (tied with the Talons). And once the Hengeyokai book came out, it was evident that the Stargazers should always have been part of that quasi-Setting. Around the end of Revised the decision was finally made to move them over there but it didn't really matter much since, being as small as they were, they usually didn't have a terribly big impact on games already.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T12:05:52-07:00","id":1083123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1083093#post1083093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. I think you could drop any individual Tribe and it wouldn't effect the overall Setting all that much. That being said, I see your point.<br /> <br /> They were just about the smallest Tribe anyway (tied with the Talons). And once the Hengeyokai book came out, it was evident that the Stargazers should always have been part of that quasi-Setting. Around the end of Revised the decision was finally made to move them over there but it didn't really matter much since, being as small as they were, they usually didn't have a terribly big impact on games already.</div> </div> </div> </div>The size of a tribe generally has never been an issue with how popular a tribe is. But yeah,I think them being a non-entity in Hengeyokai was weird. Especially as that would be the group they would be the closest to. Instead, they were treated as being outsiders even among -that- setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T12:23:24-07:00","id":1083135,"title":"","content":"They are a connection to a region and culture and somewhat a pop-culture trope. Some people like to play Werewolf kung-fu monks. That's enough reason to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T13:11:07-07:00","id":1083148,"title":"","content":"I've only read a few werewolf books and never played a game so you may take what i say with a grain of salt as there are a lot of things i probably didnt understand quite right. <br /> But for me the interest towards the stargazer were never about the werewolf kung-fu monk side of things. It was more that, to my understanding, they had an approach towards rage that was very different from the rest of the tribes. I saw it as a weird mix of denial, acceptance, mastery and transcendence of Rage that made the tribe appealing to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T13:22:34-07:00","id":1083154,"title":"","content":"Quite true, I naturally oversimplified it. Honestly, the philosophical side is much more interesting to me too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T13:50:37-07:00","id":1083169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1083148#post1083148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've only read a few werewolf books and never played a game so you may take what i say with a grain of salt as there are a lot of things i probably didnt understand quite right.<br /> But for me the interest towards the stargazer were never about the werewolf kung-fu monk side of things. It was more that, to my understanding, they had an approach towards rage that was very different from the rest of the tribes. I saw it as a weird mix of denial, acceptance, mastery and transcendence of Rage that made the tribe appealing to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is cool ^^<br /> <br /> For me, it always felt that they weren't given the kind of issues with Rage that Children of Gaia or Furies had. That, and them being so heavily monastic with the celibacy feels a bit weird for a creature that is half-wolf. That, and they never truly felt part of either Hengeyokai OR Garou Nation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T14:28:28-07:00","id":1083181,"title":"","content":"I think the Stargazers have a role in the game (though poorly implemented), but they don't really have a role as a Tribe.<br /> <br /> The simplest solution is to make them a cross-Tribal camp of Asian werewolves that takes in any Garou seeking to follow their teachings. Their low numbers can easily be attributed to the lack of in-setting popularity of their teachings. This also makes it easier on why they don't have a lot of Lupus Garou to explain their very human approach to things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T13:28:11-07:00","id":1083645,"title":"","content":"I think that Stargazers function best as an adoptive Tribe rather than a born Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T08:12:25-07:00","id":1083980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1083181#post1083181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The simplest solution is to make them a cross-Tribal camp of Asian werewolves that takes in any Garou seeking to follow their teachings. Their low numbers can easily be attributed to the lack of in-setting popularity of their teachings. This also makes it easier on why they don't have a lot of Lupus Garou to explain their very human approach to things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to run the Stargazers like that in my games. Also the Children of Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T08:47:58-07:00","id":1084504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1083181#post1083181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Stargazers have a role in the game (though poorly implemented), but they don't really have a role as a Tribe.<br /> <br /> The simplest solution is to make them a cross-Tribal camp of Asian werewolves that takes in any Garou seeking to follow their teachings. Their low numbers can easily be attributed to the lack of in-setting popularity of their teachings. This also makes it easier on why they don't have a lot of Lupus Garou to explain their very human approach to things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, given the first tribebook, it is very much fitting for them to be like that.<br /> <br /> But in general, another issue I have with them is that they never felt they were involved in the setting. Like, if they truly had been trying to teach the Nation for centuries, why is Kailindo so obscure? Why can't other tribe say any personal feelings about them other than &quot;they talk a lot and are calm&quot;. They just... existed, apparently.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, them being a multi-tribal camp makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T09:25:30-07:00","id":1084518,"title":"","content":"I like them. Every rule has an exception: most Garou are berserkers, but Stargazers are meditant monks and tranquil shamans. They're the exception to the normal Garou mindset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T09:28:34-07:00","id":1084519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1084518#post1084518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like them. Every rule has an exception: most Garou are berserkers, but Stargazers are meditant monks and tranquil shamans. They're the exception to the normal Garou mindset.</div> </div> </div> </div>The conflict being that if you have Rage, you're still a berserker, and you have to have Rage to be a werewolf, so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T09:32:40-07:00","id":1084522,"title":"","content":"I like the Gazers, given the unique way they approach their Rage and their perspective of the Weaver.<br /> <br /> The Tribe that doesn't sit right for me are the Children of Gaia - they have cause without culture. I just made them into a multi-tribal Camp, which I think fits their themes better. It also accounts for their absence in the parts of the world where their goal is realized without them looking like they're bad at their job. It's just Garou in East Asia or Africa who believe in CoG agenda of unity join the Beast Courts or Ahadi (respectively) instead. The CoG specifically exist as an organization to pursue that goal where it hasn't been realized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T10:32:33-07:00","id":1084555,"title":"","content":"Yes, they cover a broad ethnicity and a conceptual place<br /> <br /> <br /> Now Fianna and Get I'd question the need for. I'll also point out the Dead/fallen tribes seem to exist purely to fall/die. I mean the white Howlers were large enough to be a tribe when their whole territory was part of a small island(at that point Hakken are a tribe!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T12:19:40-07:00","id":1084627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1084555#post1084555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, they cover a broad ethnicity and a conceptual place<br /> <br /> <br /> Now Fianna and Get I'd question the need for. I'll also point out the Dead/fallen tribes seem to exist purely to fall/die. I mean the white Howlers were large enough to be a tribe when their whole territory was part of a small island(at that point Hakken are a tribe!)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hakken are a bit of a special case, since their island ended up very densely populated, which also allowed them to pull ahead on homid numbers alone to become as populous as a tribe in their own right..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T13:06:55-07:00","id":1084653,"title":"","content":"Eh. Ultimately the problem is that the game doesn't really want to decide what a Tribe really is.<br /> <br /> Is a Tribe an ethnicity where any philosophical teachings are incidental to familial status?<br /> <br /> Is a Tribe a way to define purpose within the large portfolio of duties the Garou take on for themselves, and relatedness simply stems from like minded individuals building tight knit communities over time?<br /> <br /> Because which Tribes seem superfluous is very linked to how you way those aspects to how the game has defined the different Tribes. Some Tribes are very much ethnicity first, others are philosophy first, and some are balanced in the middle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T13:16:12-07:00","id":1084662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1084653#post1084653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. Ultimately the problem is that the game doesn't really want to decide what a Tribe really is.<br /> <br /> Is a Tribe an ethnicity where any philosophical teachings are incidental to familial status?<br /> <br /> Is a Tribe a way to define purpose within the large portfolio of duties the Garou take on for themselves, and relatedness simply stems from like minded individuals building tight knit communities over time?<br /> <br /> Because which Tribes seem superfluous is very linked to how you way those aspects to how the game has defined the different Tribes. Some Tribes are very much ethnicity first, others are philosophy first, and some are balanced in the middle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Should the game make a definite decision on what a tribe is?<br /> <br /> United States is a country based on ideas, while Germany is a country based on Culture. It is possible to be culturally German and still consider yourself an citizen of the US.<br /> <br /> You don't see tribes overlap that way, but I can see tribes such as Glasswalkers, Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia, Black Furies, etc transcend culture and focus on principles and ideas, while tribes such as Fianna, Get of Fenris, Uktena, etc define themselves by culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":".  Clarifying what country I am talking about. 04-27-2017, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T13:31:18-07:00","id":1084671,"title":"","content":"I think the game would be better with a clear vision of what makes something a Tribe vs. similar concepts such as Camps, Houses, and Lodges. This isn't a matter of setting building or anything, but a matter of game design. If you don't have a good idea of what X is, how do you make a good X? The Tribes started as rather shallow stereotypical archetypes, that were fleshed out in various directions to give them more depth. However those attempts lacked any guidance based on what makes something a Tribe, so they're all over the place in application.<br /> <br /> I'm also really not sure what you mean with the countries example. All countries are based on ideas and culture. An American can move to Germany and become a Germany citizen, without stopping to consider themselves American culturally. Citizenship and cultural identity are different things that may or may not overlap within a given individual's beliefs.<br /> <br /> Not every American or German holds the belief that every citizen of their country is a &quot;real&quot; member of that country just because they have legal status.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T18:23:30-07:00","id":1084798,"title":"","content":"Well, a lodge in W:tA is pretty easy to define - there are only two of them, and only the Silver Fangs have them. (^VVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T18:55:29-07:00","id":1084810,"title":"","content":"Same with Houses.<br /> <br /> I actually think they're ideas that should have been bigger, because it would imply a more solid idea of what a Tribe is. If ever Tribe worked like the Fangs, you'd have a core philosophy (&quot;We're the Tribe of Kings, born to rule the Garou Nation and claiming the best kin; in the form of royal families in our human kin&quot;), supported and cooperative specialists in the finer points of that philosophy (Lodges), regional variants linked to specific ethnic groups (Houses), and the less formal or less openly acknowledged sub-groups within the Tribe (Camps).<br /> <br /> Though if you did this, I think it would be hard to avoid turning most of the current Tribes into Houses or Lodges inside a smaller number of combined groups. But that actually makes a bunch of things easier, because it would make Tribes much larger in numbers, so filling out all those Tribal sub-groups isn't as hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T17:53:30-07:00","id":1085250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1084653#post1084653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. Ultimately the problem is that the game doesn't really want to decide what a Tribe really is.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I see it, Tribes are really large packs.<br /> You can live and die in your native pack or be adopted in another.<br /> You can be apart from your pack, but you will still remain a member of the pack.<br /> <br /> It's not really a thing of culture, genealogy or whatever. It's only US (the pack) and THE OTHERS (not-the-pack), it's a really wolf-ish thing, strengthened by the common totem.<br /> Then the &quot;human&quot; side of the Garou took care of the rest, developing different cultures, different ceremonies, different philosophies and so on (even the Red Talons' human side did it).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T15:46:43-07:00","id":1085922,"title":"","content":"No tribe is actually &quot;needed&quot;. It all depends on what you think each tribe contributes to the game you run. That is based on both personal preference and how that tribe is depicted in your individual chronicles. I've seen tribes like the Bone Gnawers in certain chronicles completely suck and be uninteresting, and others by different STs where they are awesome and contribute a lot to the game.<br /> <br /> I do think there are some problems with the Stargazers, but that has little to do with how the tribe was originally presented in the corebook versus how they will developed in the subsequent tribebooks.<br /> <br /> Originally as written, the Stargazers were not written as exclusively Asian. The description was:<br /> 1) A minority of Garou opposed to the Impergium (pre-Concord) choose to withdraw into seclusion<br /> 2) They sought a life of contemplation and enlightenment, and there withdrew to remote locations (1st edition also mentioned &quot;or journeying to the Far East&quot; which is the only Asian connection)<br /> 3) They gained their name because they could be seen at night alone staring into the night sky.<br /> 4) They seek the truth and inner peace.<br /> 5) They are a tribe of philosophers, mystics, and spiritualists.<br /> <br /> That's it. Nothing that says they are predominantly in Asia. Or that they know some strange form of kung fu or stick fighting. Instead, they are just monks and ascetics seeking internal wisdom and enlightenment (which is a feature pretty universal in all complex societies).<br /> <br /> The expectation seemed to be that in any remote location around the world, you might see a Stargazer. In first and early second edition material, you could find a Stargazer in New York City, or in Swiss Alps. They might have some kind of tie to the Far East, or they might not. Certainly the stereotype inspired by some kind of Buddhist monk was an early and popular trope, but it wasn't the only one.<br /> <br /> It's just that the tribe was developed way too strongly in that way until it got to the point where if you weren't Tibetan, you weren't really a Stargazer but some kind of weirdo. In truth, the Stargazers everywhere should be the weirdos, and the Far East should have plenty of other Garou available to them (Silver Fangs, Shadow Lords, Glass Walkers, Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia, and even some others).<br /> <br /> This is something I can easily correct for in my chronicles.<br /> <br /> To me, a more serious problem is the weird status of the Chimera totem. It is supposed to be a totem of enigmatic mystery, but its connections to dreams (and therefore Fae/Changelings) and the Greek myth of the Chimera monster sit very uneasily with the tribe's purpose. While it is certainly true that the term Chimera is used to describe impossible things, that has no basis in the actual legends of Chimera. Furthermore, despite Bellerophon riding Pegasus to slay Chimera in myth, nothing seems to ever be made of this in discussion between Stargazers and Black Furies. It certainly makes no sense for an &quot;Asian tribe&quot; to have as its totem a creature from Greek mythology!<br /> <br /> The tribe would be better served in my opinion, if it had a different totem. Perhaps Sphinx (because of its famous riddles), or if you were trying to go with an animal/creature not bound to a specific culture, then perhaps something like Butterfly (because of its changing nature and the mysteries of death and rebirth), Elephant (prodigious in memory and wisdom), or even Crane. Or if you want a more solitary animal, perhaps something like Praying Mantis which lives mostly by itself and has lots of mythological connotations and legends about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 09-12-2017, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T16:07:59-07:00","id":1085929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1085922#post1085922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No tribe is actually &quot;needed&quot;. It all depends on what you think each tribe contributes to the game you run. That is based on both personal preference and how that tribe is depicted in your individual chronicles. I've seen tribes like the Bone Gnawers in certain chronicles completely suck and be uninteresting, and others by different STs where they are awesome and contribute a lot to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is much truth in that. You could easily pare the game down to 5 or 6 tribes, if you wanted. But I like all of them, and find a lot of potential in each. Admittedly, some inspire ideas more easily than others, but there's never really been a time when I said, &quot;I just can't think of anything to do with X&quot;. <br /> <br /> As for their Totem, I believe Chimera is meant in the sense of &quot;an illusion of fabrication of the mind; especially: an unrealizable dream&quot; (from Merriam-Webster), rather than the Greek mythological beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T07:30:10-07:00","id":1086188,"title":"","content":"I love the Stargazers, they nearly tie with the Get for me but the Get narrowly beat them because Fenris is a niftier Totem.<br /> <br /> I believe they bring a lot to the table, and them being few in number is more a feature and not a bug.<br /> <br /> They are a tribe like anyone elses.<br /> <br /> W20 seems kind of contradictory with how they portray Werewolf Populations, they seem to have werewolves out the butt and don't really emphasize the they are rare and dying out issue. I definitely don't get a Red Talons only have 400 members and Stargazers Number half that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T18:12:07-07:00","id":1086405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1085929#post1085929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for their Totem, I believe Chimera is meant in the sense of &quot;an illusion of fabrication of the mind; especially: an unrealizable dream&quot; (from Merriam-Webster), rather than the Greek mythological beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that is what they are going for in terms of what the totem can do and what tribe is about, but of course the only creature they could use for that name is the Greek mythological monster which is an extremely poor fit.<br /> <br /> The more I think about it now, Mantis would probably be the most relevant totem.<br /> <br /> 1) Mantises are solitary creatures which is what Stargazers are.<br /> <br /> 2) Mantises are known for their excellent camouflage so they can hide from both their prey and predators. Some Mantises appear like sticks; others like flowers; some like ants; and even more simply by crypsis coloration. That fits with the whole illusion theme.<br /> <br /> 3) Mantises are known for their hunting skills to the extent that have inspired entire martial arts traditions named after them.<br /> <br /> 4) Mantises have real world folklore that associates them with wisdom - from the fact they look like the pray, serve as a pyschopomp, or have various supernatural powers. They also transform since they molt and &quot;abandon&quot; one form to another as they go through their instars. While not as dramatic as though insects which have a pupa stage, it can still serve as a totem of spiritual change and development.<br /> <br /> 5) Mantises are fairly ubiquitous covering India, the Middle East, North Africa, and southern Europe.<br /> <br /> The one major flaw is that they aren't particularly known for being in remote places (like mountains) and are mainly tropical and sub-tropical, not temperate or cold where wolves generally are. But overall, I think it's a good fit. I may end up keeping Stargazers in terms of descriptions and mechanics, but simply state Mantis is the totem in my game. That may help clear up any confusion that arises because of Chimera (I've never had anyone complain about Chimera as totem, but it's always bothered me).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T18:27:03-07:00","id":1086409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1086405#post1086405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree that is what they are going for in terms of what the totem can do and what tribe is about, but of course the only creature they could use for that name is the Greek mythological monster which is an extremely poor fit.<br /> <br /> The more I think about it now, Mantis would probably be the most relevant totem.<br /> <br /> 1) Mantises are solitary creatures which is what Stargazers are.<br /> <br /> 2) Mantises are known for their excellent camouflage so they can hide from both their prey and predators. Some Mantises appear like sticks; others like flowers; some like ants; and even more simply by crypsis coloration. That fits with the whole illusion theme.<br /> <br /> 3) Mantises are known for their hunting skills to the extent that have inspired entire martial arts traditions named after them.<br /> <br /> 4) Mantises have real world folklore that associates them with wisdom - from the fact they look like the pray, serve as a pyschopomp, or have various supernatural powers. They also transform since they molt and &quot;abandon&quot; one form to another as they go through their instars. While not as dramatic as though insects which have a pupa stage, it can still serve as a totem of spiritual change and development.<br /> <br /> 5) Mantises are fairly ubiquitous covering India, the Middle East, North Africa, and southern Europe.<br /> <br /> The one major flaw is that they aren't particularly known for being in remote places (like mountains) and are mainly tropical and sub-tropical, not temperate or cold where wolves generally are. But overall, I think it's a good fit. I may end up keeping Stargazers in terms of descriptions and mechanics, but simply state Mantis is the totem in my game. That may help clear up any confusion that arises because of Chimera (I've never had anyone complain about Chimera as totem, but it's always bothered me).</div> </div> </div> </div>The other major flaw is that the Ananasi probably hobbled that Incarna horribly during the Insect Wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T18:51:05-07:00","id":1086415,"title":"","content":"It's also very weaver-esk imo. Could possibly step on glass Walker toes. I could see chimera taking in mantis after the great insect war and adding it to its brood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 05-01-2017, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T06:28:19-07:00","id":1086583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1086415#post1086415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also very weaver-esk imo. Could possibly step on glass Walker toes. I could see chimera taking in mantis after the great insect war and adding it to its brood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all insects are weavery. What about the butterfly? It's a traditional symbol of change and inner peace. Also it's spelled &quot;esque&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T08:10:11-07:00","id":1086640,"title":"","content":"Flea is also a Gaian Incarna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T11:28:45-07:00","id":1086719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1086405#post1086405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree that is what they are going for in terms of what the totem can do and what tribe is about, but of course the only creature they could use for that name is the Greek mythological monster which is an extremely poor fit.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No. I mean the Stargazer totem isn't supposed to be a &quot;creature&quot; of any sort; Their totem is literally a construct of pure thought that doesn't exist in any physical form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T12:30:12-07:00","id":1086739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1086719#post1086719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. I mean the Stargazer totem isn't supposed to be a &quot;creature&quot; of any sort; Their totem is literally a construct of pure thought that doesn't exist in any physical form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I think people get too hung up on the name. Chimera as presented in WtA material is obviously a different beast altogether than the rapacious creature slain by Bellerophon.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the Stargazers serving a being of thought, a spirit that lives in dreams. Chimera inhabits the subconscious thoughts of its followers, underlining the tribe's cerebral and contemplative nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T17:40:46-07:00","id":1087417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1086719#post1086719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. I mean the Stargazer totem isn't supposed to be a &quot;creature&quot; of any sort; Their totem is literally a construct of pure thought that doesn't exist in any physical form.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1086739#post1086739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. I think people get too hung up on the name. Chimera as presented in WtA material is obviously a different beast altogether than the rapacious creature slain by Bellerophon.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just the name. They use the actual picture of the creature as well. Someone who is just introduced to the game is going to clearly think that the totem is the actual Chimera of legend, just like some other tribes have totems of other legendary creatures like Fenris Wolf or Pegasus.<br /> <br /> Now I agree with you that the way Stargazers and their totem has developed, that the totem clearly has no connection of the actual mythological creature it is named after. But if that is the case why use the name and look in the first place?<br /> <br /> I think there is clearly a problem when you go that route. It's like the old saw about that the Greek poet Homer never existed, instead the Iliad and Odyssey were written by a different man with the same name.<br /> <br /> If the totem is clearly a spirit completely different than Chimera, then use another name for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 05-04-2017, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T21:19:56-07:00","id":1087504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1087417#post1087417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the totem is clearly a spirit completely different than Chimera, then use another name for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I don't really see why; things can share names. I think calling the totem 'Chimera' sounds better than calling it 'Tulpa' or 'Psychic construct.' I think it is interesting that it is differentiated from the classical Chimera, and, as others have noted, 'Chimerical' can be described as 'existing only as the product of unchecked imagination' or even 'fantastically visionary.'<br /> <br /> Seems appropriate enough to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T23:00:32-07:00","id":1087529,"title":"","content":"Also, it wouldn't be different by very many letters. Chimerica, or something of that sort, perhaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T13:44:43-07:00","id":1087898,"title":"","content":"Well, chimera is an actual word for the concept. As for the art, I think that's most likely a case of either a) the art notes given to the artist didn't clarify just what this &quot;chimera&quot; thing was supposed to be and so he/she defaulted to what everyone first thinks of when the name is mentioned, or b) having no idea how to represent something that doesn't have a physical form, someone just said &quot;screw it, draw the monster&quot;. Or maybe it was both. ::shrug::","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T18:16:42-07:00","id":1100668,"title":"","content":"I think the Stargazers work well as Garou who actually argue being a bunch of violent rage-filled bullies is a dumb way of life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T18:46:27-07:00","id":1100674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1100668#post1100668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Stargazers work well as Garou who actually argue being a bunch of violent rage-filled bullies is a dumb way of life.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then they'd have to have a completely different renown system, which they don't, unless they're in the Beast Courts or Ahadi. Generally, it's the cubs who argue that, in most of the tribes as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T21:25:44-07:00","id":1100699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1100674#post1100674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then they'd have to have a completely different renown system, which they don't, unless they're in the Beast Courts or Ahadi. Generally, it's the cubs who argue that, in most of the tribes as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>They still believe in defeating the Wyrm, they just take an entirely different view of Rage and self-control than other Garou. Mind you, Rage is a source of power for all Garou so the fact the Stargazers are quixotic to other members of their race is deliberate. Even the Children of Gaia, for all their idealism, believe it's important to be violence filled animals. Stargazers, by contrast, see Rage as a weakness and control over it as a weakness.<br /> <br /> To which you might argue, &quot;But there's no way such Garou would ever be able to get along with other Garou who are motivated by rage in all things.&quot;<br /> <br /> And which, yes, Revised said, &quot;Yes, in the end, they found out they had more in common with the Fera courts and left the Garou Nation.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mostly use the Stargazers as an opportunity to show that Garou don't HAVE to blood-soaked berserkers. But if they AREN'T, they may actually be going against their purpose under Gaia.<br /> <br /> It's a neat little philosophical question.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T21:42:30-07:00","id":1100702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1100699#post1100699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They still believe in defeating the Wyrm, they just take an entirely different view of Rage and self-control than other Garou. Mind you, Rage is a source of power for all Garou so the fact the Stargazers are quixotic to other members of their race is deliberate. Even the Children of Gaia, for all their idealism, believe it's important to be violence filled animals. Stargazers, by contrast, see Rage as a weakness and control over it as a weakness.<br /> <br /> To which you might argue, &quot;But there's no way such Garou would ever be able to get along with other Garou who are motivated by rage in all things.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm saying that their elders are still mired in tradition. Very much the opposite of what you're attributing, actually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And which, yes, Revised said, &quot;Yes, in the end, they found out they had more in common with the Fera courts and left the Garou Nation.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mostly use the Stargazers as an opportunity to show that Garou don't HAVE to blood-soaked berserkers. But if they AREN'T, they may actually be going against their purpose under Gaia.<br /> <br /> It's a neat little philosophical question. </div> </div> </div>No, a question of game and setting. The bent of the Stargazers, and indeed all tribes, is best if it's orthogonal to the goal in some form, not defining it entirely.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T22:08:36-07:00","id":1100710,"title":"","content":"I don't get your point. At all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T02:57:57-07:00","id":1100759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1100699#post1100699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stargazers, by contrast, see Rage as a weakness and control over it as a weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... not really? The Stargazers don't see Rage as a weakness, and absolutely seek control over it. They see Rage as dangerous, and attempting to master just by stoking it as weakness. They view strength as achieving tranquility despite Rage and seek transcendence to a balanced state where tranquility and Rage are experienced in harmony with each other as they fulfill their duties as warriors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And which, yes, Revised said, &quot;Yes, in the end, they found out they had more in common with the Fera courts and left the Garou Nation.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Well, mostly left. Some didn't (of an already small Tribe), and W20 walked this back anyway to have this be more of an impending possibility. Of course, being members of the Garou Nation or throwing in with the Beast Courts doesn't really address the thread topic of their viability as a Tribe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mostly use the Stargazers as an opportunity to show that Garou don't HAVE to blood-soaked berserkers. But if they AREN'T, they may actually be going against their purpose under Gaia. </div> </div> </div>I find this rather boring myself, because it means everyone else must be a blood-soaked berserker. Get Rabagash are way better at this to me because being a Fenrir that bucks the Tribal image of being a the most bloody of berserkers and fighting with swift cunning elegance over brute force calls into question what the Garou's true purpose is by fulfilling their Auspice purpose so adamantly.<br /> <br /> I frankly hate it when one Tribe needs to edge out concepts in other Tribes to protect their thematic niche. If the rest of the Garou need to be blood-soaked berserkers for the space for the Stargazer's Middle Way, then I can do without the Stargazers as a Tribe.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1100710#post1100710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get your point. At all.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm interpreting currently:<br /> <br /> 1) Elder Stargazers don't argue that, &quot;being a bunch of violent rage-filled bullies is a dumb way of life.&quot; Because that argument is something they recognize is futile and counterproductive. It is the young Stargazers that are still only at a shallow understanding of their Tribe's philosophies that would make this argument. The older traditional Stargazers value the wisdom that Rage has to offer, and understand that Rage is an inherent part of their nature, and thus do not begrudge others that cope with it in their own ways. These elders also still value Glory as warriors and understand that this duty is shared by all Garou, combined with the burden of Rage, and to judge the other Tribes as the externally look, &quot;bullies,&quot; is a failure of the compassion they seek to temper their Rage with.<br /> <br /> 2) &quot;Neat philosophic questions&quot; aren't good things to define the Tribes. Tribal culture should be interesting by being variations to the core idea of the Garou without losing being Garou, rather than being defined solely by a philosophic quirk that is opposed to the Garou concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T08:18:20-07:00","id":1100851,"title":"","content":"Well, to each their own but I strongly disagree. I also don't get your reasoning other than, &quot;I don't like it.&quot; Quirky philosophical points describes just about every single tribe of the Garou. Also, you've pretty much put down my favorite tribe in the Children of Gaia since their existence requires the Garou to be bloody berserkers as they WOULDN'T BE NEEDED otherwise. It's also a major part of the games' themes that the Garou have severe issues with the fact they've all committed horrible atrocities. The idea they're not all blood-soaked berserkers kind of requires the Imperium, War of Rage, and the fact they're a warrior race in constant battle as powered by their anger to not happen.<br /> <br /> On my end, each of the Tribes provides the players an opportunity to play a different kind of character by giving them an archetype to build off of. The Peacebringers, the Warriors, Wonder Woman, The Snooty Royals, the Backstabbing Evil Chancellors, and so on.<br /> <br /> Everyone has Theruges but if you want to be a THE Garou Wizard, you go to the Uktena.<br /> <br /> The Stargazers work in addition to being &quot;Kung Fu Wolves&quot; the enlightened spiritual types.<br /> <br /> I think it's awesome but to each their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-06-2017, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T16:11:09-07:00","id":1101003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1100851#post1100851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, to each their own but I strongly disagree. I also don't get your reasoning other than, &quot;I don't like it.&quot; Quirky philosophical points describes just about every single tribe of the Garou. Also, you've pretty much put down my favorite tribe in the Children of Gaia since their existence requires the Garou to be bloody berserkers as they WOULDN'T BE NEEDED otherwise. It's also a major part of the games' themes that the Garou have severe issues with the fact they've all committed horrible atrocities. The idea they're not all blood-soaked berserkers kind of requires the Imperium, War of Rage, and the fact they're a warrior race in constant battle as powered by their anger to not happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, their existence requires that there be a combination of arrogance and unwillingness to back down that gives rise to terrible errors in the past and a not really repentant attitude towards the entire thing. Which there is; Garou are still hypocritically calling the Mokole the very image of the Wyrm while simultaneously venerating totems like Typhon (a storm dragon) and Firedrake (which is basically Smaug from The Hobbit).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On my end, each of the Tribes provides the players an opportunity to play a different kind of character by giving them an archetype to build off of. The Peacebringers, the Warriors, Wonder Woman, The Snooty Royals, the Backstabbing Evil Chancellors, and so on. </div> </div> </div>Everyone is &quot;the Warriors&quot;, though, and Shadow Lords haven't been Evil Chancellors since first edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Everyone has Theruges but if you want to be a THE Garou Wizard, you go to the Uktena. </div> </div> </div>Their gifts provide a very specific form of magical prowess. Because that's what the Gifts that everyone has are... magic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T18:06:23-07:00","id":1101049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1101003#post1101003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, their existence requires that there be a combination of arrogance and unwillingness to back down that gives rise to terrible errors in the past and a not really repentant attitude towards the entire thing. Which there is; Garou are still hypocritically calling the Mokole the very image of the Wyrm while simultaneously venerating totems like Typhon (a storm dragon) and Firedrake (which is basically Smaug from The Hobbit).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah.as in the revised Silver Fang tribebook, Byeli tells Albrecht that the Garou were justified in launching the War of Rage against the Fera. Albrecht angrily calls out Byeli for his cultural posturing.<br /> <br /> <b>Albrecht:</b><i> Look, I've been patient and respectful and all, but ... this is a lot like the kind of bullshit I've heard for years, about how we can do no wrong, and it's always the other guys' fault that things went bad. Do we have a congenital defect, a complete inability to 'fess up to our mistakes?</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Everyone is &quot;the Warriors&quot;, though, and Shadow Lords haven't been Evil Chancellors since first edition. </div> </div> </div>Yeah and the Stargazers are the measured calm warrior-monks. Basically, if you want to play a werewolf Jedi.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their gifts provide a very specific form of magical prowess. Because that's what the Gifts that everyone has are... magic. </div> </div> </div>My point is that you have some tribes who excel things better at Auspices than others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T18:30:54-07:00","id":1101444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1101049#post1101049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah.as in the revised Silver Fang tribebook, Byeli tells Albrecht that the Garou were justified in launching the War of Rage against the Fera. Albrecht angrily calls out Byeli for his cultural posturing.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that reminds me about how the Fangs follow Wyvern but would still decry the Mokole... which makes them like the Dragonslayers from a certain D&amp;D campaign setting where you play dragons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah and the Stargazers are the measured calm warrior-monks. Basically, if you want to play a werewolf Jedi. </div> </div> </div>It's a bit more involved than that, and has less jedi, on account of the emphasis of Gift additions like Wuxing. They don't have to be like monks; in fact, they're probably more comfortable with Daoist practices than Buddhist ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My point is that you have some tribes who excel things better at Auspices than others. </div> </div> </div>Except that being a Theurge isn't like being a magic-user. And here, the D&amp;D analogies break down, on account of how Theurges are shamans, and there have been umpteen different mechanical writeups for that archetype across D&amp;D's history...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T21:52:13-07:00","id":1102190,"title":"","content":"Lore aside, have you ever played as one? Seems easy to be a Stargazer when you hear their tales in the tribebooks. I mean, some Stargazers let themselves to be killed 'cause its their fate, its how it is supposed to be. They go by rules that seems not necessary by those in power, that's how I see Stargazers in the Garou Nation. So, yes, they are needed. More likley needed somewhere in the Umbra, but still.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13101-ntrlz","name":"Ntrlz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13101_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T13:46:44-07:00","id":1103257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1100668#post1100668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Stargazers work well as Garou who actually argue being a bunch of violent rage-filled bullies is a dumb way of life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think every tribe works for that. <br /> <br /> (I think that's even one of the main themes of the revised Get of Fenris book. Their idea of Strength is not what the stereotypes of them would suggest.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T13:55:22-07:00","id":1103259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083058-are-the-stargazers-a-needed-tribe?p=1101049#post1101049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah and the Stargazers are the measured calm warrior-monks. Basically, if you want to play a werewolf Jedi.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's actually the archetypical <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?61031-WoD-Child-of-Gaia-Ahroun&amp;p=1142075#post1142075\" target=\"_blank\">Child of Gaia Ahroun</a>. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}